==================================================
              Test Division
==================================================

PERSON 1 - MODEL PACKAGE
Focus: Testing the game's objects.

  PlayerTest.java
    - Test player creation, health, and attributes.

  RoomTest.java
    - Test room creation, connections, and contents.

  MonsterTest.java
    - Test monster creation, health, and attributes.

  ItemTest.java
    - Test item creation, properties, and types.

  InventoryTest.java
    - Test adding, removing, and retrieving items.


--------------------------------------------------


PERSON 2 - ENGINE & EVENTS PACKAGES
Focus: Testing how the game works.

  ENGINE:

  CombatTest.java
    - Test fighting monsters and combat outcomes.

  GameEngineTest.java
    - Test overall game functionality and progression.

  InteractionTest.java
    - Test interactions with objects and entities.

  MovementTest.java
    - Test moving between rooms and locked doors.


  EVENTS:

  CombatEventTest.java
    - Test results generated by combat.

  InteractionEventTest.java
    - Test results generated by interactions.

  MovementEventTest.java
    - Test results generated by movement.


--------------------------------------------------


PERSON 3 - RULES & CONFIG PACKAGES
Focus: Testing game rules and setup.

  RULES:

  DamageRuleTest.java
    - Test damage calculations.

  QuestRuleTest.java
    - Test quest progression and completion.

  TrapRuleTest.java
    - Test trap activation and effects.


  CONFIG:

  GameConfigTest.java
    - Test game world creation and initialization.


==================================================
              SHARED RESPONSIBILITIES
==================================================

EVERYONE:
  - Write JUnit 5 tests.
  - Test normal scenarios and edge cases.
  - Use @ParameterizedTest where appropriate.
  - Check code coverage using EclEmma.
  - Run PIT mutation testing.
  - Improve tests to catch surviving mutations.
  - Make sure all assigned tests pass.